## BUG-01: Identity hijack via TOFU race during initial discovery
# Severity: HIGH
# Files: consensus/MeshNode.cpp:803-807, consensus/MeshNode.cpp:1029-1032
#
# TOFU accepts the first public key for a given peer_id. An attacker on-LAN
# who broadcasts a DISCOVERY or ANNOUNCE signed with their own key under a
# victim's node_id before the legitimate node's beacon arrives permanently
# pins the attacker's key. Subsequent legitimate beacons are rejected:
#
#   if (!peer_pem.empty() && !existing.public_key_pem.empty()
#       && existing.public_key_pem != peer_pem) {
#       std::cerr << "[SECURITY] TOFU key change REJECTED for " << peer_id;
#
# Attacker can then cast PBFT votes as the victim, trigger false isolation.
#
# Fix: Bind identity to boot proof (TPM), require OOB key distribution, or
# add witness threshold where N existing peers vouch for a new key.

## BUG-02: m_message_history grows unbounded — eventual OOM
# Severity: HIGH
# Files: consensus/PBFT.hpp:509, consensus/PBFT.hpp:405-425
#
# detect_equivocation() appends to m_message_history at line 425:
#   history[msg.sequence_number] = msg_hash;
# There is NO eviction, pruning, or size limit. cleanup_stale_rounds()
# cleans m_rounds and m_vote_registry but NOT m_message_history.
# No TTL-based or cap-based eviction anywhere.
#
# At 1,000 msgs/sec × 5 peers × ~100 bytes = ~500KB/sec = 1.8GB/hour.
# Also affects m_rate_limits (line 511) which also has no periodic cleanup.
#
# Fix: Add age-based or cap-based eviction (keep last N sequences per sender;
# or add timestamp and evict entries older than ROUND_TTL_SEC).

## BUG-03: TelemetryBridge sandbox degrades silently to unsafe state
# Severity: HIGH
# Files: telemetry/TelemetryBridge.cpp:219-270
#
# All sandbox functions use "warn on failure, continue without" pattern.
# apply_fs_isolation() at line 223:
#   " — continuing WITHOUT sandbox (WebSocket will still work)"
# Same in apply_uid_drop (line 254), apply_seccomp_filter (line 279).
# If /var/empty doesn't exist (common in minimal containers), chroot fails
# silently. Child runs with uid+gid unchanged + no seccomp.
#
# The child accepts WebSocket connections from the network. A uWS
# vulnerability gives attacker root-level code execution.
#
# Fix: Make sandbox failures fatal (_exit(1)). Add --unsafe flag for dev.
# Ensure Dockerfile stage 2 creates /var/empty (currently line 57 does).

## BUG-04: mTLS with no CA loaded — TLS connections are NOT verified
# Severity: HIGH
# Files: net/TransportLayer.cpp:68-76, consensus/MeshNode.cpp:98-102
#
# m_tls_config.verify_client = true and enable_mtls = true are set, but
# m_tls_config.ca_path is never assigned (defaults to "").
# TLSContext::TLSContext at line 73 only loads CA if ca_path is non-empty:
#   if (!m_config.ca_path.empty()) { load_ca_certificate(); }
# Without load_ca_certificate, SSL_CTX_set_verify is never called.
# SSL_get_verify_result() in get_connection_info() returns X509_V_OK
# for ANY certificate — including self-signed, expired, or attacker certs.
#
# MeshNode connects TLS to peers (line 843-847) and accepts TLS connections
# (tls_acceptor_loop). Peer TLS fingerprints are tracked via TOFU but the
# TLS socket itself never validates remote certificates.
#
# Fix: Set m_tls_config.ca_path in MeshNode constructor, or PIN peer certs
# and use SSL_CTX_set_cert_verify_callback for custom verification.

