## BUG-14: Atomic relaxed ordering without documented correctness model
# Severity: LOW
# Files: cell/InferenceEngine.hpp:24, common/StateJournal.hpp:151,
#        consensus/MeshNode.hpp:99
#
# All atomic operations use std::memory_order_relaxed:
# - m_last_score.load/store (InferenceEngine)
# - m_seq.fetch_add (StateJournal)
# - m_sequence_number.fetch_add (MeshNode)
#
# These are correct for monotonic counters with no ordering dependencies,
# but no code comments explain WHY relaxed is safe. Future refactoring
# that introduces a dependency (e.g., reading sequence before init is done)
# would silently break on ARM/POWER.
#
# Fix: Add /* memory_order_relaxed */ comments explaining safety rationale.

